      "math_academy_id": "e-2293",
      "problem": "Anthony says $400$ words in $6$ minutes. If he speaks at a steady pace, what statement describes the unit rate?",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of spoken words to minutes is ${\\color{blue}400}:{\\color{red}6}.$ So we start with the ratio $400:6$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}400}}{{\\color{red}6}}\n$$\n\nWe can reduce this fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{400 \\div 2}{6 \\div 2} = \\dfrac{200}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Anthony said $\\dfrac{200}{3}$ words per minute.",
